  "exitSteps": [],
  "answer": "Save is on while the page differs from how it loaded and off once it is the same again, by the Undo button and by Cmd+Z alike. A blank section alone: on; one Undo takes the section away and Save goes off; Redo brings both back. A Text added: one Undo takes the Text, Save stays on (the blank section is left); the next takes the section, Save off. A Text written in (ab), or Write pressed and nothing typed: the same, Save off only at the last step, when the section is gone. So CAP-Y2KEYS2's 'Undo button, just added' read Save on because its blank section was still there, not by a rule of its own. Read twice: CAP-Y2SAVEUNDO2 agrees on every read's save, sections and has. Two earlier reads of the same steps with controls in place of has (commit 8028b463) agree too; controls were left out here, as they follow where the mouse last sat.",
  "ours": "The same rule: ours compares the page with the saved one (app/src/editor.js, savedJson), so no app change. The replay (scripts/lib/text-replay.mjs) had no step for the oracle's blank Add Section; it now adds a blank section at the page's end (fe.addSection), an undo step of its own, and text-check drops the CAP-Y2KEYS2 save known miss.",
  "pressed": "Undo and Redo by name (pressNamed). Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z as keys. The section by Add Section, Add Blank (blank). Nothing saved: Exit Without Saving."
}
